diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index bf04b4f..b066595 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -66,6 +66,7 @@ DM_ICON	path	`=<image>` gives `build_ipa.sh` another app icon (default the `icon
 DM_IMPORTS	diagnostic	When set, logs each import the loader binds to a host function and each forced takeover
 DM_KBD	switch	`=<text>`: the system keyboard returns that text as OK without showing an input box; unset with no window, it returns cancel
 DM_KBD_PLAYER	switch	`own` makes the Mac keyboard player 1 on its own, with controllers from player 2 on (by default the first controller shares player 1 with the keyboard)
+DM_KEYMAP	switch	`=<map>` such as `A=40,B=38,LS_UP=126`: which Mac key (virtual key code, -1 none) does each Switch button, stick direction or Shake (names A B X Y LS RS L R ZL ZR PLUS MINUS LEFT UP RIGHT DOWN LS_UP LS_LEFT LS_DOWN LS_RIGHT RS_UP RS_LEFT RS_DOWN RS_RIGHT SHAKE; default J K U I, F G, Q E Z C, Return Tab, arrows, WASD, Space, `front_mac.m`); Shift with a D-pad key still turns the right stick; Mac only
 DM_KEYS	switch	Scripted input: `<seconds or f<frame>>:<key>[+key][~hold or ~f<frames>][*count/interval],…` presses buttons, sticks, touches and `Shake` at those times; `=@<file>` reads the steps from the file
 DM_LANG	player	Game language as a language code (default `en-US`; the iOS app sets the one the IPA was packed with)
 DM_LAUNCHER	switch	`0` skips the iOS settings screen or the Mac settings window and starts the game at once, with the saved choices (on the Mac also `--no-launcher`)
